  "query_preview": "..(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 400 AM EST SUN NOV 1 2026\n\nUpper ridging shifts across eastern KY and sections of the Southeast\nMonday night to Tuesday. Meanwhile, the upper level trough moves \ninto the Central Conus and approaches the OH Valley from the west.\nRecent deterministic GFS and ECMWF runs and GEFS/EPS means develop\na closed low by late Tuesday, but then differ in the track and how\nlong it is maintained and the downstream evolution. The common\ntheme of deterministic and ensemble guidance is that the axis of\nthe 500 mb trough should remain west of eastern KY into at least\nFriday. Also, there is consensus in the guidance on bringing a\nlead shortwave trough into the OH Valley on Wednesday which crosses\nthe area by late Wednesday night or early Thursday. At the same \ntime, a sfc low pressure system should track from the Central and \ninto the eastern Conus and through the OH Valley. As this system \ncrosses the area, 00Z LREF from the 31st has mean PW rising into \nthe 1.2 to 1.4 inch range on Wednesday afternoon/evening or \nroughly into at least the 90th to 97th percentile for early \nNovember. This system should bring the potential for more \nwidespread rainfall to the region from Wednesday into Thursday. \nSome locally heavier rainfall is not out of the question if there \nwere to be any training given the degree of anticipated moisture. \nWPC has placed western portions of the CWA in a marginal risk \n(Level 1 of 4) for excessive rainfall for Day 4.\n\nThunder cannot be ruled out as the midweek system passes though \ninstability will be limited with MUCAPE peaking at 250 J/kg or \nless per 00Z LREF. Winds may also become a bit gusty with the \nmidweek system in the Tuesday night to Wednesday evening period, \nwith the strongest gusts most probable in the higher terrain near \nthe VA border. ENS based probabilities for wind gusts over 40 mph \nare maximized in the 20 to 30 percent range near the VA \nborder/harlan County per the 00Z LREF. Otherwise, chances for rain\nlinger until the 500 mb trough axis crosses the area around the \nlate Friday to early Saturday timeframe. \n\nTemperatures will be mild on Tuesday, on the order of 10 to 15 \ndegrees or so above normal for highs and remain mild until the\nfront crosses the region at midweek. Temperatures trend colder to\nend the week as the trough moves across the area.",
